  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Meet, turn and attack 1v1",
  "description": "Two lines outside the sidelines level with the free-throw line. Everyone in one line has a ball (attackers); the defenders are in the other line. The first player in each line steps in: the attacker dribbles and the defender runs towards the middle. They meet at the free-throw line and slap hands in the air.\n\nThen the attacker turns and dribbles at full speed to half-court, touches the line and turns to attack the basket. The defender runs under the basket and then closes out on the dribbler. Then it is live 1v1 – both may rebound and play on until a basket is scored (or after 2–3 shots). Switch lines and roles.\n\nVariant: whoever loses goes to (or stays in) the defenders' line. Put a time limit on each possession. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Dribble with your eyes up – find your partner's hand without looking at the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Defence: meet the ball far out, shorten your steps at the end and contest every shot and drive."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Attack: don't stop – use your speed and attack the defender's lead foot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Box out after the shot and fight for the rebound."
    }
  ],
